\title{essurvey2: download data from the 'European Social Survey' API}
\description{
\code{essurvey2} is a client for the 'European Social Survey' ('ESS') data API at
\url{https://api.ess.sikt.no}. It discovers what is published through the 'ESS'
metadata catalogue, downloads data files as 'Apache Parquet', and returns
\link[data.table:data.table]{data.table::data.table} objects.
}
\section{Configuration}{

Every request to the data API must carry a user ID, which the ESS uses to
record download statistics. Obtain one by logging in at
\url{https://ess.sikt.no/en/api}, then store it as the \code{ESS_USER_ID}
environment variable. See \code{\link[=ess_user_id]{ess_user_id()}} and \code{\link[=ess_set_user_id]{ess_set_user_id()}}.
}

\section{Finding data}{

Nothing in this group downloads survey data, so these are cheap to call.
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ess_rounds]{ess_rounds()}} — published ESS rounds and their main data file
\item \code{\link[=ess_data_files]{ess_data_files()}} — every data file in a round
\item \code{\link[=ess_data_file_info]{ess_data_file_info()}} — a data file's DOI and coverage
\item \code{\link[=ess_countries]{ess_countries()}}, \code{\link[=ess_country_rounds]{ess_country_rounds()}} — country coverage
\item \code{\link[=ess_themes]{ess_themes()}}, \code{\link[=ess_theme_rounds]{ess_theme_rounds()}} — questionnaire themes
\item \code{\link[=ess_variables]{ess_variables()}} — variable-level metadata
\item \code{\link[=ess_series]{ess_series()}} — ESS and related survey series
}
}

\section{Downloading data}{

\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ess_round]{ess_round()}} — one or more rounds as a \code{data.table}
\item \code{\link[=ess_all_rounds]{ess_all_rounds()}} — every published round, stacked
\item \code{\link[=ess_country]{ess_country()}} — one country across rounds
