\section{Cache}{

Downloads can be cached on disk between sessions. The default location is in
your own filespace, so the package asks before writing there and falls back to
the session's temporary directory when it may not. The cache is capped and
trimmed oldest-first. See \code{\link[=ess_cache_dir]{ess_cache_dir()}}, \code{\link[=ess_cache_list]{ess_cache_list()}} and
\code{\link[=ess_cache_clear]{ess_cache_clear()}}.
}

\section{Differences from the essurvey package}{

The earlier \code{essurvey} package scraped the ESS website and parsed SPSS or
Stata files with \code{haven}. Those endpoints no longer exist. Two consequences
are visible in this package's interface:
\itemize{
\item A round's respondents come as one integrated file, so \code{\link[=ess_country]{ess_country()}}
downloads a whole round and filters it locally rather than fetching a
country file. (A handful of countries held out of an integrated file do have
their own file; see \code{\link[=ess_data_files]{ess_data_files()}} with \code{kind = "country"}.)
\item Parquet columns arrive as plain integers and strings. Value labels live in
the metadata catalogue (\code{\link[=ess_variables]{ess_variables()}}), not in the data file.
}
}

